er, and Weld Counties\n\nWHEN...400 PM Tuesday August 18 to 400 PM Wednesday August 19\n\nIMPACTS...Ozone Action Day Alert is now in effect for the Front\nRange Urban Corridor.  Hot and sunny weather with light winds and\nlimited potential for afternoon storms will allow ozone to reach\nlevels that are Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups on Tuesday and\nWednesday. The highest ozone concentrations are most likely in the\nsouthern and western portions of the Denver Metro area.   For\nColorado air quality conditions, forecasts, and advisories, visit:\nhttps://www.colorado.gov/airquality/colorado_summary.aspx   If\npossible, please help us reduce ozone pollution by limiting\ndriving gas and diesel-powered vehicles until at least 4 p.m.\nWednesday, August 19, 2026. Colorado is also addressing ozone\npollution through state policies. For more information about\nhealth impacts and how ozone pollution forms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone-pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-19T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Broomfield, CO; Boulder, CO; Douglas, CO; Larimer, CO; Jefferson, CO; Weld, CO; Denver, CO; Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bcd88b1b66192e2d43a08e5556c874386ead632c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bcd88b1b66192e2d43a08e5556c874386ead632c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-19T11:32:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 191132 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 532 AM MDT Wed Aug 19 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Isolated storms today, though chances of stronger storms shift to the south. - Warming and drying trend to end the week, before monsoon moisture attempts to return Sunday into early next week. && .DISCUSSION /Through Tuesday/... Issued at 140 AM MDT Wed Au","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-19T09:13:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Today and tonight... Isolated showers and thunderstorms are expected this afternoon and evening. Temperatures will be near normal this afternoon, with minimum RHs around 20% to 35% across much of the area. No elevated fire weather conditions expected. LONG TERM DISCUSSION...Thursday through Sunday... Warmer and generally drier conditions are expected Thursday and Friday. Temperatures","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"ccr01","station_name":"Cherry Creek Reservoir","distance_km":11.5,"soil_temp_5cm_f":69.55,"soil_temp_15cm_f":76.01,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":1.15,"wind_speed_mph":3.51,"air_temp_f":62.83,"relative_humidity":0.767,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/ccr01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KAPA","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"SPECI KAPA 191210Z VRB04KT 7SM -RA FEW015 OVC100 17/13 A3023 RMK AO2 RAB07 OCNL LTGICCC DSNT S CB DSNT S MOV E P0002 T01720128","temp_f":63,"wind_dir":"VRB","wind_kt":4,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":7,"cover":"OVC","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1023.8,"observed":1787141400,"raw_taf":"TAF KAPA 191131Z 1912/2012 16011KT P6SM VCSH BKN120 FM191300 18008KT P6SM SCT120 FM191500 VRB06KT P6SM SCT110 FM191800 05009KT P6SM FEW080 SCT120 PROB30 1921/2001 VRB20G30KT -SHRA BKN080 FM200100 17011KT P6SM FEW080 SCT120 FM200300 18012G20KT P6SM SCT120 FM200700 21007KT P6SM FEW120","url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids=KAPA&hours=0"},"airgradient":{"pm25":0,"aqi_pm25":0,"sensor_count":5,"distance_km":19.7,"max_distance_km":23.2,"name":"5 outdoor